  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "Marking – 3v5, defend the slot",
  "description": "Three defenders play against five attackers on half the rink. The attackers try to score on a big net with a goalie. The defenders try to prevent and block shots and counter on two small nets by the red line. In front of the net, cones mark the slot – the area where shots are most dangerous.\n\nAttackers score: goal from the slot 3 pts, goal from a one-timer where the puck passed through the slot 2 pts, other goals 1 pt.\nDefenders score: goal on a counter 1 pt, winning the puck in the slot 1 pt, blocked shot 2 pts.\n\nNot to scale. The goalie is not drawn.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Mark tightly when your player is near the slot – you can give more room when they are far away."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Stand on the side of your opponent that is closest to the net and the puck."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Cut off passing lanes into the slot with your stick on the ice."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Steer the pressure so the attackers end up outside the slot."
    }
  ],
